[{:seon.task/name "a-value-already-serialized-is-stored-as-it-is"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: a written Leaf is serialized twice on Jolt: once in Datahike to hash its content address (``datahike.index.persistent-set/leaf-content-uuid``), once in konserve when the value is stored (the FaslSerializer through ``konserve.impl.defaults/direct-bytes``). The second pass is about 50k ticks of a one-datom commit (measured 2026-11-11). Datahike cannot hand the store the bytes it already made: konserve has no path for a value already serialized. Correct: konserve accepts bytes already in the store's own serialized form for a value (unwrapped for write hooks, refused when the store's serializer is another), and Datahike hashes exactly the bytes that are written (they carry each Datom's cached hash today, so the hashed form and the stored form must be made the same first). Upstream's shape first: read whether upstream konserve or Datahike already has such a path before adding one. Where: the konserve fork and ``datahike.index.persistent-set/store``. Proof when built: a commit serializes each written node once (a counter in a test), same addresses for the same content, a deep `verify-chain` :ok. Should cost: one serialization a node; saves about 50k ticks of a one-datom commit."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-store-key-costs-one-digest"
  :seon.task/plan "Measured 2026-11-11: of the 200k ticks konserve's multi-assoc spends on the 23 values of a one-datom commit, `key->store-key` is 40k (hasch's uuid of each key, to name its file or LMDB key), the meta maps' serialize and zstd 10k, `meta-update` 6k, the associated data built for an encryptor that is not configured 7k, headers and the rest about 24k, the LMDB transaction 18k. An open pays `key->store-key` too: 46 keys. Correct, smallest first: associated data is not built when no encryptor is configured; a store key is computed with one digest on Jolt, the same value as today (the hasch path on Jolt was already cut from 15.4 KB to under 9.9 KB a key by reading the digest array in place). Upstream's own konserve first: these are in files upstream owns, so each change is written in its style and only where upstream has none. Proof when built: the write of n small values costs a stated number per value, flat in n. Should cost: under 3k ticks a value outside serialization and compression."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{}}
]
